{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/597729-headshot-or-heartshot","id":597729,"title":"Headshot or Heartshot","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-20T20:21:27-07:00","id":597729,"title":"Headshot or Heartshot","content":"I was wondering a simple question.<br /> <br /> Aside from the fact that a stake in the heart can do a specific effect on vampires, I was asking myself if shooting a vampire in the face with a shotgun, going full auto with an AK47 at the heart area, or shooting with a sniper right in the forehead, would be considered lethal instead of bashing ?<br /> <br /> The official rule is that firearm delivers bashing to vampires, but what do you think ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T20:36:47-07:00","id":597754,"title":"","content":"I'd rule for my games the shotgun to the face would get lethal. The sniper shot to the head would probably get a Tilt or Condition but not lethal, except with certain kinds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-20-2015, 11:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T20:39:44-07:00","id":597758,"title":"","content":"I'd rule that a shotgun to the face would deal aggravated to humans anyway, so yeah, it'd be lethal to vampires in my games. The sniper shot to the forehead? That'd probably cause the Stunned Tilt, but it'd be bashing damage to a vampire. The AK to the chest? Just plain bashing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T20:45:09-07:00","id":597793,"title":"","content":"My take is that if a vampire's head or heart has been turned into a fine red mist, they are dead. Supernatural physiology still has it's limits, and anything that effectively turns a part of your anatomy that you need to survive into vapor is <b>FATAL</b>. Likewise, dropping a Mask into a vat of molten steel like the T-100 kills it. There are some things you just can't survive, unless it's a Scion game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T00:54:34-07:00","id":598041,"title":"","content":"The question is if what you're talking about is needed to survive. It seems counterintuitive nowadays to say a brain isn't needed, but come on, we're talking about an undead being. The only think you can be sure a vampire needs to survive is blood. Anything else is arguable, and should be defined by chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T01:25:53-07:00","id":598053,"title":"","content":"Decapitation kills them, so I think they need their heads. Likewise, I'm pretty sure having their hearts removed is fatal. (Unless certain Disciplines are being used)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T08:25:25-07:00","id":598384,"title":"","content":"I will probably rules that the vampire, needs to have his brain, attached, to his heart. Imean... the body does that... decapitation cuts this connection. The heart can be greatly damaged and the brain too, and they will still function, but severing the connection by cutting it, or removing completly one of the two... should kills them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T09:04:25-07:00","id":598419,"title":"","content":"New headcanon: A wooden stake to the brain does the exact same as one to the heart, but almost nobody knows this because it's so hard to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T11:50:22-07:00","id":598587,"title":"","content":"I will keep to the stake on the heart because I like the idea of a mystical weakness not following any biological logic. The decapitation could be because of the brain, or just a piece of the brain (like the cerebellum), or any other aspect of the head, or the neck itself (like in Highlander), or just for the metaphysical weight of the whole head: as long as anyone can recognaise a head, even if a really broken one, the vampire is alive.<br /> <br /> Since the vampire is a supernatural creature, scientific logic is moot. Of course, you CAN use it on your game and it CAN be fun. But isn't at all a necessity. Even the heart isn't required per se. You could rule that a severed vampire's heart still works for him, and that only a wooden stake through it will paralize the vampire. And even that if the heart is destroyed, the vampire's body just makes a new one on the following night, not because it is a necessary structure, but because it does have enough metaphysical weight to force itself on existence again. As part of the Curse, the vampire doesn't need a heart, but he does need a WEAKNESS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T12:31:47-07:00","id":598620,"title":"","content":"Personally, I would actually say that decapitation just puts a vampire into torpor - even if your head is a fine mist, you can come back, same as regular torpor through damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T12:33:08-07:00","id":598621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/597729-headshot-or-heartshot?p=598419#post598419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New headcanon: A wooden stake to the brain does the exact same as one to the heart, but almost nobody knows this because it's so hard to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to some folklore, driving a nail into the skull would keep a vampire from rising,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T12:49:10-07:00","id":598627,"title":"","content":"I run games where vampires are virtually immortal unless you destroy the brain and the heart by breaking them into multiple pieces. Basically it takes either an extra step in a normal damage to push them over the edge into final death or some spectacular end that destroys them completely. I mostly run mixed games and this is partly to protect the PC Kindred from final death and partly for dramatic purposes in bringing back recurring villains or threats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T15:21:14-07:00","id":598718,"title":"","content":"Well, according to the book, there is an example at page 33, where a certain vampire meet the final death by being decapitated with a guillotine in 1780. In other words, it seems to be canon that complete decapitation delivers final death, according to the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T18:11:52-07:00","id":598811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/597729-headshot-or-heartshot?p=598587#post598587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will keep to the stake on the heart because I like the idea of a mystical weakness not following any biological logic. The decapitation could be because of the brain, or just a piece of the brain (like the cerebellum), or any other aspect of the head, or the neck itself (like in Highlander), or just for the metaphysical weight of the whole head: as long as anyone can recognaise a head, even if a really broken one, the vampire is alive.<br /> <br /> Since the vampire is a supernatural creature, scientific logic is moot. Of course, you CAN use it on your game and it CAN be fun. But isn't at all a necessity. Even the heart isn't required per se. You could rule that a severed vampire's heart still works for him, and that only a wooden stake through it will paralize the vampire. And even that if the heart is destroyed, the vampire's body just makes a new one on the following night, not because it is a necessary structure, but because it does have enough metaphysical weight to force itself on existence again. As part of the Curse, the vampire doesn't need a heart, but he does need a WEAKNESS.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget are there ancient mekhet who were mummified before embraced so they are missing their brains.<br /> All they have Sawdust and myrh. How much damage does shooting that do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T18:46:23-07:00","id":598853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warriorshaman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/597729-headshot-or-heartshot?p=598718#post598718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, according to the book, there is an example at page 33, where a certain vampire meet the final death by being decapitated with a guillotine in 1780. In other words, it seems to be canon that complete decapitation delivers final death, according to the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>This could be a case of correlation without causation. A vampire had his head removed with a guillotine and subsequently died. That doesn't necessarily mean that decapitation automatically causes final death for all vampires. I mean, you could theoretically kill a vampire with a punch if his health track has enough damage on it to begin with, but that doesn't mean all vampires die from being punched.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T20:35:51-07:00","id":598969,"title":"","content":"Let's apply lore to this: Aside from Stephanie Meyer, pretty much everyone who has ever written about vampires has said decapitation=death. And I'm pretty sure even Sparkle Vamps die if decapitated by another vampire, or a werewolf. Combat should have consequences in WoD. And that goes for all splats. Silver kills werewolves, but it's not the only way, unless you want to be silly:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/8SlWegS2sS0\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/8SlWegS2sS0\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/8SlWegS2sS0\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/8SlWegS2sS0 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T20:46:37-07:00","id":598977,"title":"","content":"Ok, that little youtube movie was funny !<br /> <br /> Of course that decapitaion might not be what put him at final death... but lets be honest...<br /> <br /> In the book, it is written that he meet final death under a guillotine. Maybe he was already beaten up... and decapitation put him down for the count... But I never saw in any story, a vampire with full health, getting decapitated, then starting to fight... to be taken down to final death with punches and kicks. <br /> <br /> If decapitation does not put all vampire to final death, it will put them into torpor at least...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T22:03:23-07:00","id":599033,"title":"","content":"I really think it's just a matter of &quot;any damage that's enough to decapitate a vampire is enough damage to kill them normally, too.&quot;<br /> <br /> If decapitation does 20L worth of damage, then no vampire is going to survive it. If a vampire does survive it, then it wouldn't decapitate.<br /> <br /> Correlation vs causation and all that. The damage kills them and decapitates. The decapitation doesn't kill them.<br /> <br /> Of course, Resilience could easily have a vampire survive a shotgun blast to the face that removes their head. That's what it does. Lets you survive while still showing the effects of the damage you negated.<br /> <br /> Of course, I'd probably also put them in Torpor for it. They lose the functionality of completely removed limbs, after all, even with Resilience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T05:37:33-07:00","id":599242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/597729-headshot-or-heartshot?p=598969#post598969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's apply lore to this: Aside from Stephanie Meyer, pretty much everyone who has ever written about vampires has said decapitation=death. And I'm pretty sure even Sparkle Vamps die if decapitated by another vampire, or a werewolf. Combat should have consequences in WoD. And that goes for all splats. Silver kills werewolves, but it's not the only way, unless you want to be silly:<br /> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/8SlWegS2sS0\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/8SlWegS2sS0</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Decapitation is THE method for Sparkle Vamps to die, just for the record. Yeah, I saw the movies. Yes, they're horrible. The second-to-last is outright offensive. But I digress.<br /> <br /> People writ about vampires for a looooooong time. Some legends about blood-sucking monsters or undeads are as old as writting itself. Those legends are much more varied than current steriotip vampires. In the Middle Ages, some people tought the only way to kill a vampire would be to exumate him, stake his heart, cut-off his head and fill his mouth with blessed bread and water. Them set the entire thing on fire. Failure in any step would be a sure way for the creature to come back.<br /> <br /> You are forcing a rule where none is needed. No, there are NO necessary logic on that. The only rules we need are the ones in the book that make the game work. Anything else can be flavoured by the ST.<br /> <br /> I'm NOT saying you shouldn't declare a decapitated vampire dead. I'm saying you should be open to possibilities. A given chronicle can benefit of strangely tough vampires, able to survive almost anything. This plays well to the trope of the Undead Unnatural Monster. The thing can live without any given piece of the body. It can't even be sure of what it realy needs for survival. Imagine the personal horror of an extreme identity crisis: how can you be sure of who you are when you find nothing in you is necessary for the Beast to go on? A non-Vampire PC can have the hell scared off him just by witnessing the creature shrugging off all kinds of descriptive damage.<br /> <br /> And all that without any balance issue, because unless you want to make decapitation your PCs favourite method for problem-solving, the main source of death in the system is, still, damage. And damage calculation won't be changed by decapitation. Or, at least, it shouldn't.<br /> <br /> Of course, you can let the vampires with as much as humane functions as you like. It can ALSO play well on some chronicles. Be it for the sake of playing sci-fi biology or to work the metaphisical properties of a human body.<br /> <br /> Just let things open. Use your preferred answer, if you like, but there are no reason at all to argue its better than anyone else's. Or to close your mind so much about eventual changes.<br /> <br /> The effect of decapiation with Resilience for me could be just the loss of sight, smell and hearing, rendering the vampire only able to perceive his surroundings by touch or preternatural senses. Oh, and he obviously can't talk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T11:54:14-07:00","id":599672,"title":"","content":"In a lot of folklore it can be easy to prevent a vampire from rising (Torpor) but difficult if not impossible to permanently destroy them (final death). Typically, the way I play it is that any vampire can be brought back from &quot;final&quot; death via certain rites if you have access to their remains (even ashes) and enough blood. This may require mass human sacrifice, the sacrifice of one or more of the vampire's childer, or even draining their sire, but it's always possible. Vampire society is not generally aware of this, hence the concept of &quot;final&quot; death, but it is a truth of the Kindred condition. This creates options for bringing back PCs and important NPCs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Giles:</b> Buffy, I've never heard of a revivification ritual being successful.<br /> <b>Buffy:</b> But you've heard of them? Thanks for the warning. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T12:58:54-07:00","id":599706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/597729-headshot-or-heartshot?p=598419#post598419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">New headcanon: A wooden stake to the brain does the exact same as one to the heart, but almost nobody knows this because it's so hard to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? Brain is bigger than Heart, generally. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T00:00:10-07:00","id":600244,"title":"","content":"Because skull. You can get to the heart by going <i>under</i> the ribs, but the skull is almost a solid plate of bone. Your best bet is probably an eye socket or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T11:13:53-07:00","id":600748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/597729-headshot-or-heartshot?p=600244#post600244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because skull. You can get to the heart by going <i>under</i> the ribs, but the skull is almost a solid plate of bone. Your best bet is probably an eye socket or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes... Missed the <i><b>Wooden Stake </b></i>reference. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Of course, the game does not really care as staking (whether Heart or your Headcanon Head) is equally difficult in that sense. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T11:19:31-07:00","id":600772,"title":"","content":"I appreciate it's just headcanon, though I'm unsure if that was a pun, but I'd still keep it to just the heart. It's more poetic.<br /> <br /> The blood is the life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T11:49:22-07:00","id":600803,"title":"","content":"Game mechanics are an abstraction for the sake of play, not a comprehensive representation of how things function in the setting.<br /> <br /> If a person is decapitated in the background, they die, there's no need to try and break down exactly what the damage infliction is.<br /> <br /> If you're playing a vampire (or somebody who is fighting one), then you can't just make a called shot to decapitate; it has to do sufficient damage within the combat system to actually play out that narrative. This goes for anybody, really.<br /> <br /> If you fill a vampire's health track with aggravated damage just using your fists, you've probably fulfilled that &quot;fully reduced them to a ruined pulp/hacked them to pieces&quot; method for Final Death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T12:17:48-07:00","id":600831,"title":"","content":"If you fill a vampire's health track with aggravated damage just using your fists every other vamp in a five mile radius is probably going to be playing dead too, because <i>dayum</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T14:06:47-07:00","id":600963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/597729-headshot-or-heartshot?p=600831#post600831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you fill a vampire's health track with aggravated damage just using your fists every other vamp in a five mile radius is probably going to be playing dead too, because <i>dayum</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankenstein Ferrum in Torment could do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T14:30:28-07:00","id":600974,"title":"","content":"Technically they'd be using some other dude's fists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T16:00:53-07:00","id":601012,"title":"","content":"Does damage still roll over?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T18:35:09-07:00","id":601222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/597729-headshot-or-heartshot?p=600974#post600974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically they'd be using some other dude's fists.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;They're mine NOW!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T19:24:52-07:00","id":601310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/597729-headshot-or-heartshot?p=601012#post601012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does damage still roll over?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be strange if it didn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T10:37:00-07:00","id":601972,"title":"","content":"The reason vampires take bashing damage from weapons is that they don't have vital organs or a proper circulatory system. What causes lethal damage is an amount of damage that actually compromises the structural integrity of their bodies. A point-blank shotgun blast to the face is singled out as a possible exception, not because vampires rely on the proper functioning of brain tissues for their survival the way mortals do, but because a wound like that is going to shred them to the point where it's hard for them to function in general. A simple small-caliber bullet to the head isn't going to do much, since it's not like a hole in their brain will slow them down, but turning their entire head into pulp will.<br /> <br /> A vampire isn't essentially different from a Strix\u2014both are effectively possessing a corpse through supernatural power\u2014but the vampire identifies with the corpse and can't just drop it and fly off to find another (usually). A Strix doesn't share that self-identification and is happy to run the body into the ground.<br /> <br /> On that logic, the rule that impaling a vampire's heart will paralyze them is really just a specific bane shared by the entire species, not the result of anything physiological.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T11:31:44-07:00","id":602039,"title":"","content":"The blast of a shot-gun is already represented by the damage caused given its statistics as a weapon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T07:11:10-07:00","id":603796,"title":"","content":"I'd play it straight by the rules. Firearm damage is lethal, downgraded to bashing. I wouldn't allow someone to use a called shot to upgrade damage on a mortal to aggravated and I wouldn't allow it to upgrade damage from bashing to lethal on a vampire.<br /> <br /> Remember that combat is an abstraction. Even if you get an exceptional success on a headshot from a sniper rifle, unless that shot <i>also</i> filled their damage track full of lethal then it was just some form of grazing shot and not a bullet-between-the-eyes scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T09:24:32-07:00","id":603889,"title":"","content":"&quot;Playing it straight by the rules&quot; includes upgrading extreme trauma. I think a bullet to the skull counts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T09:45:52-07:00","id":603900,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but by the rules it's things that destroy large quantities of tissue that are upgraded to aggravated damage - hand in a wood chipper, laying on a grenade, anything that reduces large chunks of the body to pulp. I'd say a shotgun blast at close range would probably count, but a .22 round probably wouldn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T11:12:06-07:00","id":603965,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Vampires don't need or use their internal organs. Brain included. I think the heart is an exception because of the &quot;heartblood&quot; that Diablerie drinks being the core of them, but that may even be taking it too literally.<br /> <br /> Vampires seem to be more interested in the amount of mass that's damaged, not where the damage occurs. Kind of like the sort of zombies that don't get killed by a headshot, rare as they are.<br /> <br /> A single bullet probably shouldn't get the damage upgrade unless it's, like, an anti-material rifle that leaves holes the size of your head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T18:29:56-07:00","id":610232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/597729-headshot-or-heartshot?p=603965#post603965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Vampires don't need or use their internal organs. Brain included. I think the heart is an exception because of the &quot;heartblood&quot; that Diablerie drinks being the core of them, but that may even be taking it too literally.<br /> <br /> Vampires seem to be more interested in the amount of mass that's damaged, not where the damage occurs. Kind of like the sort of zombies that don't get killed by a headshot, rare as they are.<br /> <br /> A single bullet probably shouldn't get the damage upgrade unless it's, like, an anti-material rifle that leaves holes the size of your head.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clearly the heart is important, otherwise the stake shouldn't work. Kidneys? No. Liver? No. Digestive tract? MAYBE the stomach, as a place to store unused blood. MAYBE. But the heart and head are essential.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yeah, but by the rules it's things that destroy large quantities of tissue that are upgraded to aggravated damage - hand in a wood chipper, laying on a grenade, anything that reduces large chunks of the body to pulp. I'd say a shotgun blast at close range would probably count, but a .22 round probably wouldn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about a .50 Cal? I'd link a picture, but it's pretty gory.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T20:08:58-07:00","id":610300,"title":"","content":"Nothing special happens if you hit the heart with anything that isn't a wooden stake. A bullet to the heart does not cause Torpor. Neither does a steel rod. It's a bane.<br /> <br /> And there's still really no indication that the head has any significance to a vampire beyond being where their sensory organs and ability to feed reside.<br /> <br /> A vampire's body is a meat suit. Nothing inside of it matters except the Vitae and &quot;heartsblood.&quot; All that matters is that there's enough meatsuit left at the end of the night to regenerate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T23:18:07-07:00","id":610476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/597729-headshot-or-heartshot?p=610300#post610300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing special happens if you hit the heart with anything that isn't a wooden stake. A bullet to the heart does not cause Torpor. Neither does a steel rod. It's a bane.<br /> <br /> And there's still really no indication that the head has any significance to a vampire beyond being where their sensory organs and ability to feed reside.<br /> <br /> A vampire's body is a meat suit. Nothing inside of it matters except the Vitae and &quot;heartsblood.&quot; All that matters is that there's enough meatsuit left at the end of the night to regenerate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, what if the heart is completely destroyed? Can we get a dev to chime in on this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T03:31:31-07:00","id":610629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/597729-headshot-or-heartshot?p=610232#post610232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clearly the heart is important, otherwise the stake shouldn't work. Kidneys? No. Liver? No. Digestive tract? MAYBE the stomach, as a place to store unused blood. MAYBE. But the heart and head are essential.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think the stake in the heart is more a mystical condition that cause just paralysis. In the 2'nd ed core book is written that vitae and blood are not concentrated in some place but are absorber from tissue and bone. It's also written (p. 98) that &quot;Vampires do not naturally bleed when cut. The Vitae is possessive; it pulls the blood back to the body in the way a drop of mercury absorbs back into a pool&quot;.<br /> <br /> A classical stake of wood (like the ones seen in the movies) have a diameter big enough to completely destroy the hearth (that have the size of a cleanched fist). A close shotgun shot to the heart or to the head Definetely completely destroy brain (and most part of the head itself) or heart. But in the core book of the 2'nd ed is specifically written that a close shotgun shot to the head that destroy the brain count as lethal damage. A bullet of a normal guns no. Cut the head, if you want that it lead to final death, should have mystical and not physiological reason. Furthemore while in first edition, decapitation is clearly written leading to final death, in second edition no. The only way to lead to final death is with enough aggravated damage. Removed head could lead to torpor or immobilization until it is regrowth as a normal removed limb in my opinion. Because tecnycally if a shotgun to the head destroy the brain but deal only lethal damage, there isn't a technical reason why decapitation should kill the vampire. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T03:48:27-07:00","id":610636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/597729-headshot-or-heartshot?p=610476#post610476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, what if the heart is completely destroyed? Can we get a dev to chime in on this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just mark the damage and wait for it to grow up again when you heal said damage. You don't need it. Be happy that you can't be staked anymore for the night.<br /> <br /> Seriously, if you want to play a sci-fi version of the game, or otherwise stablish that in your game vampires work like Resident Evil zombies, go ahead. You don't need a dev to let you do so.<br /> <br /> But there are no reason for the game to work on such premisse as default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T11:45:33-07:00","id":611115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/597729-headshot-or-heartshot?p=610476#post610476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, what if the heart is completely destroyed? Can we get a dev to chime in on this?</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems like one of those things that would take filling up a sheet with aggravated to do.<br /> <br /> Like if someone punches a vampire in a chest and does 2 bashing damage, you don't describe it as the fist punching through the chest and coming out the back clutching the vampire's shriveled heart. If you manage 7 lethal in a called shot to the chest, the heart is still there just probably got a hole in it or something. But if you managed another attack that did 7 lethal after that, causing damage to wrap around to aggravated and kill the vampire, you might describe the heart as being obliterated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-01-2015, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T12:01:34-07:00","id":611128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/597729-headshot-or-heartshot?p=603796#post603796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd play it straight by the rules. Firearm damage is lethal, downgraded to bashing. I wouldn't allow someone to use a called shot to upgrade damage on a mortal to aggravated and I wouldn't allow it to upgrade damage from bashing to lethal on a vampire.<br /> <br /> Remember that combat is an abstraction. Even if you get an exceptional success on a headshot from a sniper rifle, unless that shot <i>also</i> filled their damage track full of lethal then it was just some form of grazing shot and not a bullet-between-the-eyes scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Letting people game the system to bypass the system is stupid and defeats the purpose of having a system.<br /> <br /> A shotgun does bashing in combat. Now, if a vampire decides to get clever and stick one in his mouth... It's just a reminder that the downgrading to bashing is a conventional abstraction that covers normal combat but could have exceptions in extraordinary circumstances. Sort of like how a dagger in D&amp;D does 1d4 damage, but that doesn't mean you can stand there and stab yourself in the neck with one and only take 1d4 damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T21:08:27-07:00","id":611836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/597729-headshot-or-heartshot?p=611115#post611115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That seems like one of those things that would take filling up a sheet with aggravated to do.<br /> <br /> Like if someone punches a vampire in a chest and does 2 bashing damage, you don't describe it as the fist punching through the chest and coming out the back clutching the vampire's shriveled heart. If you manage 7 lethal in a called shot to the chest, the heart is still there just probably got a hole in it or something. But if you managed another attack that did 7 lethal after that, causing damage to wrap around to aggravated and kill the vampire, you might describe the heart as being obliterated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that makes sense. I get that vampires are all &quot;<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">m</span><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">a</span><span style=\"color:#FFFF00\">g</span><span style=\"color:#800080\">i</span><span style=\"color:#FFA500\">c</span><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">a</span><span style=\"color:#EE82EE\">l</span>&quot; and junk, but that doesn't mean logic and common sense lose all meaning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T04:52:56-07:00","id":612051,"title":"","content":"Ahn... in a sense, it does, at least as far as <u>your</u> logic goes. There are no sense at all in a corpse completely dead to be affected by loss of brain or heart once it isn't affected by loss of liver or kidneys.<br /> <br /> But again, whatever works for you. Go for the system and just describe the lessened damage, because if you don't, you'll get your players gaming called shots as a means to avoid the intended difficulties. If someone really does something to guarantee a blown head, make happen whatever you think should happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T09:35:16-07:00","id":612333,"title":"","content":"I don't know if it's already been said, but the suggested rational behind lethal damage when you're hitting the head seems to predicate on 2 things: 1. that Rose implied in a blog post awhile back that metaphysically the head is the &quot;seat of consciousness&quot; in Kindred, even dead, and 2. the typical remark from the book, that grievous bodily harm can cause lethal damage to a vampire.<br /> <br /> I don't know about all this heart junk, but I assume if you're making a targetted shot against the heart and doing 5+ damage that you're hurting them p. badly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T09:14:43-07:00","id":625594,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Mangle77]<br /> <br /> Let's apply lore to this: Aside from Stephanie Meyer, pretty much everyone who has ever written about vampires has said decapitation=death. And I'm pretty sure even Sparkle Vamps die if decapitated by another vampire, or a werewolf. Combat should have consequences in WoD. And that goes for all splats.<br /> <br /> [QUOTE]<br /> <br /> If I remember correctly in Tolstoj's Vurdalak a vampire throws his head against the protagonist after he cutted its, in Bram Stoker's Dracula (at least in Coppola's one) for destroy a vampire you have to stake him and cut his head (cut it just make him wake) and, I saw just the first movie of &quot;Twilight Sparkle&quot; saga, the vampire has to be entirely destroy and burned.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/597729-headshot-or-heartshot?p=610476#post610476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, what if the heart is completely destroyed? Can we get a dev to chime in on this?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you destroy the heart the blood just spread out in chest cage, it is all there. Just some vitae and it rebuilds easily.<br /> I think even if you cut an head off a vampire and he's &quot;fresh&quot; he can keep it &quot;attached&quot; with the blood as it is a viscous fluid, then the vampire can rebuild meat and skin with vitae.<br /> <br /> I think that the stake block a vampire just because the wood &quot;drink&quot; the blood. It can be a simple explanation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7277-brighella","name":"Brighella","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T11:18:59-07:00","id":625689,"title":"","content":"I think it's not cause wood drink vitae. Even a sponge or the best scottex in commerce can't absorb all blood istantly, and even in this case, a vampire without blood can still walk till the next night when he will not have the blood to wake up and he'll fall in torpor. I think it's due to a mystical factor linked with wood. <br /> By the way I'm according with you: head cut or destroy heart don't kill vampire. Head cut could put him in torpor. In the first edition it was specifically written between the causes of death that cut the head or fill all the health box with aggravated damages lead the vamp to the final death. In the next one, in the same section the only one thing leading to final death is written to be aggravated damages.<br /> Was it just a forgetfulness??? I don't know but we can see a thing in the second edition: a lot of previous limit has been deleted. Under this light is not too weird think that the headcut has been no taken as a cause of final death anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 08-13-2015, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T19:07:36-07:00","id":626140,"title":"","content":"The use of a wooden stake through the heart was purely symbolic and owes most of its fame to the idea of Vlad the Impaler (emphasis on impaler) being destroyed by the same means he was famous for employing. Other myths required that an iron spike be driven through the heart, nailing the vampire to the ground and imprisoning (not destroying) him there. Another involved burying him at a cross roads so he wouldn't know which way to go and his confusion would prevent him from rising again. The use of holy water and wafers was associated with the power of god to purify and destroy evil. Flame is the same, consuming and purifying whatever it touches. The writers of the game just chose the most commonly known methods (thanks to Bram Stoker), then added the possibility of the others as additional banes taken by blood lines. The heart, head or whatever is based upon the symbolic beliefs of the people they come from. As for the head, medically it wasn't all that long ago they though the brain was just packing material, the heart was the focus of life. More people survived head injuries (including a four foot metal rod through the cranium) then damage to the heart.<br /> It was a tamping rod, he worked for the railroad. It was his subsequent change in personality that led to the discovery that the brain was home to the way you think.\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6084,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","user":"2ptTakrill","date":". 08-13-2015, 10:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T22:32:49-07:00","id":626341,"title":"","content":"The man you're talking about was named Phineas Gage, and the reason his case was so significant is that it effectively settled the cerebral localization debate that was still going on at the time. In other words, the midical community was well aware by that time that the brain was the seat of consciousness, they were merely arguing over whether all parts of the brain were equally important in all cognitive function, or if certain parts were responsible for certain tasks. The fact that Gage survived the destruction of a significant portion of his frontal lobe with seemingly little resulting imparment was in and of itself strong evidence in favor of the hypothesis that brain function is localized. But more importanly, his personality changed drastically after the injury, which indicated that the frontal lobe must be largely responsible for personality. This line of thought is what lead to the invention of the frontal lobotomy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T01:18:43-07:00","id":626425,"title":"","content":"And them frontal lobotomy took a story of its own. An ugly, bloody story, with its major proponent being literally a wandering lobotomy surgeon. Nasty stuff, wonderful for the WoD, shameful for reality.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't change that even on works like Bram Stoker and Anne Rice, vampires where mostly governed by mystical symbolic rules. There where some legends in witch the head was actually the target for iron nails and the like.<br /> <br /> In a quick search on the internet, I learned just now that people argue about the role of the brain on thought, reason and emotion since ancient times. The idea that just recently it was discovered as that is, itself, a legend. But it doesn't really change things. People's beliefs are more based on culture than fact, and even today the heart is usually more significant mystically. Also, no mater how much researchers postulated this possibility, things only started to become really clear on 1.780, with Luigi Galvani's studies on electrical response of muscles, and even them it took some years to prove that the electrical stimulus came from the brain. Until them, no theory on the subject could be proven.<br /> <br /> Of course, all that means nothing to the undead. They are undead, after all. Theories about mystical energies and the seat of the soul are far more relevant for them, since their bodies are already in defiance of every single natural law postulated by science. They go about without heat or circulation. Their muscles work seemly without electricity. They draw energy more from the symbol of the blood than from any physical property of it (hook for the Supernal here?). Their regeneration and their own stasis put to the ground physical laws about mass and energy. As their state curses their souls, their very existence is a blasphemy not only against most religious thoughts, but against nature itself, refusing to follow any of the laws that bound every living being on Earth from the very moment of their raising from the actual or proverbial grave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T07:19:02-07:00","id":626603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/597729-headshot-or-heartshot?p=626425#post626425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And them frontal lobotomy took a story of its own. An ugly, bloody story, with its major proponent being literally a wandering lobotomy surgeon. Nasty stuff, wonderful for the WoD, shameful for reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should watch the Movie &quot;<i><b>Sucker Punch</b></i>&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T07:52:41-07:00","id":626639,"title":"","content":"A bit late on this, but just to get the word in:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/597729-headshot-or-heartshot?p=601310#post601310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be strange if it didn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>In which case, there's nothing remarkable about beating a vampire into a no longer functional pulp by wailing on them for long enough, is there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T12:03:20-07:00","id":626777,"title":"","content":"To make a long story short, the devs chose a combination of mythic symbolism and game play. They decided filling the damage track, and the horrific injuries it represents (remember, vampires don't bleed to death) would be sufficient because staking, chopping off the head, filling the mouth with holly wafers followed by cremation, all while a priest performs funeral rites over the body was just too cumbersome to be used in a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}